[center][size=6][b]Dynamic Key Prompts[/b][/size]
[size=3]Your actual key bindings in every button prompt[/size][/center]

[center][quote][size=3][b]Early version (0.1.x).[/b] It works in all prompts I've tested, but so far only on a few setups (Russian and English game, Seamless Co-op, ModEngine2).
If something looks wrong - a prompt with a gamepad button, a wrong key, misaligned icons - please report it in the [b]Bugs[/b] tab with DynamicKeyPrompts.log and a screenshot. Every report helps![/size][/quote][/center]

Dark Souls III shows Xbox buttons in its prompts even when you play with keyboard and mouse. Other mods replace the button textures with fixed keys - which is wrong as soon as you rebind anything.

[b]Dynamic Key Prompts reads the bindings from the game itself[/b] and shows the key or mouse button you actually use - and follows your changes in the Key Bindings screen.

[b]Also available for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/darksouls2/mods/1738]Dark Souls II: Scholar of the First Sin[/url].[/b]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/1392/images/2379/2379-1790508945-703919774.jpg[/img][/center]

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Every prompt: menus, the help bar, interaction prompts ("Light bonfire", "Examine"), messages, tutorial texts, menu tabs[/*]
[*]Key and mouse icons in the style of the game, or plain text labels like [E][/*]
[*]Context aware: in menus A means [i]OK[/i], in the world it means [i]Interact[/i] - each shows its own key[/*]
[*]Mouse buttons where you bound them, Shift combinations shown as Shift + key, the camera as mouse movement[/*]
[*]Three icon themes: dark, minimal, silver[/*]
[*]Does not modify any game file - delete one DLL to uninstall[/*]
[*]Compatible with [b]Seamless Co-op[/b] and [b]ModEngine2[/b][/*]
[/list]
[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/1392/images/2379/2379-1790508945-308071769.jpg[/img][/center]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/1392/images/2379/2379-1790508941-1318930075.jpg[/img][/center]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Dark Souls III, Steam, latest update (1.15.2)[/*]
[*]Windows 10/11 64-bit[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[b]Vortex:[/b] click [i]Mod Manager Download[/i] and deploy - the files go to the Game folder.

[b]Manual:[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Steam > Dark Souls III > Manage > Browse local files > open the [b]Game[/b] folder (the one with DarkSoulsIII.exe)[/*]
[*]Copy [b]dinput8.dll[/b] and the [b]DynamicKeyPrompts[/b] folder into it[/*]
[*]Start the game as usual (with Seamless Co-op: through ds3sc_launcher.exe; with ModEngine2: through launchmod_darksouls3.bat)[/*]
[/list]
[b]Uninstall:[/b] remove the mod in Vortex, or delete dinput8.dll and the DynamicKeyPrompts folder.

[size=4][b]Settings[/b][/size]
Edit [b]DynamicKeyPrompts\DynamicKeyPrompts.ini[/b]:
[list]
[*][b]Style[/b] = icons / text[/*]
[*][b]IconTheme[/b] = dark / minimal / silver[/*]
[*][b]Labels[/b] = auto / mouse / both[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
The mod loads through [b]dinput8.dll[/b]. If another mod already uses dinput8.dll, download the optional [b]xinput1_3 loader[/b] file and use its [b]xinput1_3.dll[/b] instead.

[b]ModEngine2:[/b] the mod can also stay outside the Game folder - put dinput8.dll and the DynamicKeyPrompts folder into any folder and list that dinput8.dll in [i]external_dlls[/i] of config_darksouls3.toml. If another ModEngine2 mod replaces menu\05_Dummy.tpf.dcx, the key icons are added to that mod's version of the file. Made to work with every game language (tested with English and Russian).

[size=4][b]Playing online[/b][/size]
The mod only changes what you see: the prompt text and a copy of one menu texture file. It doesn't touch saves, params, items or stats and sends nothing over the network.
[list]
[*][b]Seamless Co-op:[/b] safe - Seamless uses its own network and doesn't connect to FromSoftware's servers.[/*]
[*][b]Official online:[/b] very likely fine for the same reasons, but like most DLL mods it hooks game code and disables the game's Arxan anti-tamper, so there is no 100% guarantee. Use at your own risk.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Troubleshooting[/b][/size]
The mod writes [b]DynamicKeyPrompts\DynamicKeyPrompts.log[/b]. For a bug report set [b]Diagnostics=1[/b] in the ini, reproduce the problem and attach the log - in the Bugs tab here or on [url=https://github.com/HappyEntity/Souls-Dynamic-Key-Prompts/issues]GitHub Issues[/url].

